---
import GraphMotif from '../GraphMotif.astro';
---

<section class="graph-idea section--panel">
  <GraphMotif class="graph-idea__motif" width={520} height={440} opacity={0.14} />

  <div class="wrap graph-idea__inner">
    <p class="kicker">The idea</p>
    <h2>A graph, not a chain.</h2>

    <p class="graph-idea__body">
      Express-style frameworks make ordering your job — what runs here, what runs there, where you wire it. Green
      Tea inverts it. You ask for the highest-level thing you need, and its dependencies resolve transitively.
    </p>

    <ul class="graph-idea__examples">
      <li>
        Need an ACL check on a user? The ACL is a step that itself needs the user. Ask for the ACL — the user is
        pulled in for you.
      </li>
      <li>Add a <code>friends</code> provider, then ask for <code>friends</code> — and the user arrives with the friend list.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="graph-idea__punch">
      This is pure composition. No other framework shows it, because no one else has the graph.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .graph-idea {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  :global(.graph-idea__motif) {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    right: -4%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    width: min(520px, 55vw);
    height: auto;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .graph-idea__inner {
    position: relative;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .graph-idea__inner h2 {
    max-width: 16ch;
  }

  .graph-idea__body {
    color: var(--dim);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .graph-idea__examples {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.1rem;
  }

  .graph-idea__examples li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .graph-idea__examples li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.55em;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--matcha);
  }

  .graph-idea__examples code {
    background: var(--base);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0.15em 0.4em;
    font-size: 0.9em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .graph-idea__punch {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--violet);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--violet) 8%, transparent);
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    :global(.graph-idea__motif) {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
